WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.100
So we're sort of looking forward to or at
least I am more so than I was looking forward

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.290
to the conventions, to the debates between
Donald Trump and Joe Biden, which are scheduled

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.009
starting in the later part of September, I
believe.

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:13.750
We're going to be covering all of them live
for sure.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:19.280
One of the things that I've said is that if
you are expecting that Joe Biden is going

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.780
to implode and he's going to just be unable
to get anything out and and so on and so forth,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.800
you're probably going to be underwhelmed.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.320
And in fact, one of the things that I've been
pointing to were some of the expectations

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.199
when the Democratic primary was down to only
Bernie Sanders and Joe Biden.

00:00:35.199 --> 00:00:38.289
You had a bunch of people on the right and
even some people on the left, kind of in the

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:43.270
pro Bernie crowd who were saying, Biden, something's
wrong with Biden.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.609
Biden's going to be unable to keep it together.

00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:47.360
Biden is going to be unable to put together
a coherent sentence.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.609
And, of course, Joe Biden did fine in order
to get the debate against Bernie Sanders.

00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:58.569
Now, it is true that the subject matter, because
it was heavily coronavirus based, probably

00:00:58.569 --> 00:01:02.120
helped Biden in in some sense.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.040
But if you were expecting Biden to be unable
to put together a sentence, you certainly

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.200
were disappointed.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.230
And I've made the same prediction about the
debates with Donald Trump.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:14.590
You have people including like Don Junior
and others on the right who are pushing the

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:19.750
Biden dementia narrative, who are claiming
that Joe Biden is barely going to know where

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.100
he is in a debate with Donald Trump.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.820
And I just don't think that's going to be
the case now in advance of this.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.390
Donald Trump has now started floating the
idea that maybe the reason Joe Biden was able

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:35.680
to hold it together in his one on one debate
with Bernie Sanders was that Joe Biden was

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.560
on some kind of drug, presumably some kind
of stimulant.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:45.240
Now, what is amazing to me about this is that
this is exactly the speculation about Donald

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:50.420
Trump, the degree of projection from Donald
Trump and Republicans.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:57.380
If you look at the RNC this week accusing
the Democratic Party and the DNC of everything

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:04.090
which they have been doing this week, accusing
the DNC of merely criticizing Trump during

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.090
their convention.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.520
Well, all they've been doing is criticizing
Joe Biden, accusing the DNC of not talking

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.680
about policy during their convention.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.709
The Republicans have not talked about any
policy during their convention.

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:21.129
And now, after years of speculation that Donald
Trump, you know, we've identified Upper Trump

00:02:21.129 --> 00:02:22.409
and Downer Trump.

00:02:22.409 --> 00:02:31.609
Upper Trump sometimes shows up at events sweaty,
speaking in a sort of manic way, dilated pupils

00:02:31.609 --> 00:02:37.159
even in front of bright lighting, sniffing,
glitching, et cetera.

00:02:37.159 --> 00:02:39.829
And then sometimes it's a downer Trump that
shows up.

00:02:39.829 --> 00:02:44.840
And, you know, the sort of casual speculation
is, is it amphetamines when it's up or Trump?

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:45.840
Is it Ben ZOS?

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:46.859
When it's Downar Trump?

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:48.930
Is it some combination of both?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:49.980
OK, whatever.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:56.549
Now, Biden Trump says he wants drug tests
before the debates because he believes Joe

00:02:56.549 --> 00:03:01.750
Biden may have been on something during his
debate with Bernie Sanders.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.959
Here's the video.

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:08.150
What nobody thought is that he was even going
to win because he had debate performances

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.150
were so bad.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.230
You know, frankly, his best performance was
against Bernie.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:18.799
We're going to call for a drug test, by the
way, because his best performance was against

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:19.799
Bernie.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:24.980
It wasn't that it was Winston Churchill because
he was it, but he was a normal, boring debate.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.069
You know, nothing amazing happened.

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:32.810
And we are going to call for a drug test because
there's no way you can't do that.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:38.919
Well, I don't know how he could have been
so incompetent in his debate performances

00:03:38.919 --> 00:03:42.819
that all of a sudden be OK against Bernie.

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:44.529
I don't mean he was good or greater.

00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:47.629
I just mean he was a normal, boring debate.

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:48.629
It was nothing.

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:49.629
You understand?

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.629
He got through it.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:56.090
Well, frankly, I thought he he was you know,
they were even more or less.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.930
And most people didn't think.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.480
And so they did something.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.480
Just something.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.349
There was no way because I watch his debates
against Carmela.

00:04:05.349 --> 00:04:07.709
There's another one that's a beauty.

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:09.010
She's she's.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:12.379
If you go by the polls, she started high and
she ended low.

00:04:12.379 --> 00:04:15.879
That's usually not a good sign, right, as
far as somebody had to pick.

00:04:15.879 --> 00:04:17.810
But against Elizabeth Warren.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.750
They ripped her apart.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:24.960
So there's a few different thoughts here.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:31.150
First of all, on the facts, should candidates
be drug tested before debates?

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.699
I don't really think so.

00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:33.919
To be perfectly frank.

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:40.030
Now, I think if you want to step back and
say we need to look at more requirements to

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.690
be president of the United States, I think
it's legally difficult.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:49.430
The one that for me would be a higher priority
than a drug test would be an actual proper

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.430
cognitive test and a neuro psyche.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.430
Val.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.599
Val, like Dr. Bandy Lee.

00:04:54.599 --> 00:04:57.800
Talk to us about a couple of weeks ago, but
maybe the.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.100
Country would decide.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.780
Presidents shouldn't be using drugs.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.599
And thus presidential candidates should be
tested for drugs.

00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:11.970
The idea of a drug test before a debate is
not particularly interesting to me.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:19.319
But the most interesting part of it is that
it is Trump who many have suspected of abusing,

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.110
whether it's amphetamines or some other type
of upper.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.060
And again, it's all speculative.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.740
But the idea that now Trump is saying Biden
should be tested.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.460
What I hear is projection.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:33.400
The constant projection from Donald Trump
of the last four years has trained me to think

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:39.300
if Trump is pointing to something, if Trump
is raising the idea, if it occurs to Trump

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:45.010
that Biden's performance may have been enhanced
by some kind of stimulant or something else,

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.199
it seems implicit that Trump is talking about
stimulants.

00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:53.220
I immediately go to is Trump thinking about
that because it applies to him.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:07:12.330
And I'm curious to hear what you think about
this.

